{"name":"Winterkeep","status":"ok","title":"Winterkeep","pageId":10787,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\" role=\"region\">\n\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Maps_of_Winterkeep\" title=\"Category:Maps of Winterkeep\">Gallery</a></nav>\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Winterkeep</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">the <a href=\"/wiki/Hordelands\" title=\"Hordelands\">Hordelands</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Northeast_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Northeast Faerûn\">northeast Faerûn</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Winterkeep\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Winterkeep\">Inhabitants of  Winterkeep</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Winterkeep\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Winterkeep\">Organizations in  Winterkeep</a></nav>\n</aside>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Winterkeep</b> was a ruin located on the southern tip of the <a href=\"/wiki/Yal_Tengri\" title=\"Yal Tengri\">Yal Tengri</a>. East of Winterkeep were the <a href=\"/wiki/Glittering_Spires\" title=\"Glittering Spires\">Glittering Spires</a>. \n</p>\n<div aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\" class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\"><input class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" role=\"button\" style=\"display:none\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"toctitle\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the surface, only rubble remained, but the extensive subterranean passageways and chambers remained mostly intact. The royal family and their servants retreated beneath the surface during winter storms; as a result these halls were comfortably furnished.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>To the <a href=\"/wiki/Vil_Adanrath\" title=\"Vil Adanrath\">Vil Adanrath</a>, Winterkeep was known as \"<i>Iket Sotha</i>\".<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FF-p60_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FF-p60-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Winterkeep was built as a nobleman's estate, in the days of <a href=\"/wiki/Raumathar\" title=\"Raumathar\">Raumathar</a>. It later became a retreat for the royal family. After the fall of the empire, Winterkeep gradually fell to ruins.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1374_DR\" title=\"1374 DR\">1374 DR</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Gelugon\" title=\"Gelugon\">gelugon</a> <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVWx0YWVsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\" title=\"Ultael (page does not exist)\">Ultael</span> enslaved several <a href=\"/wiki/Ice_troll\" title=\"Ice troll\">ice troll</a> warbands and started to attempt to make a fiefdom for himself. He sent several warbands out to raid along the <a href=\"/wiki/Golden_Way\" title=\"Golden Way\">Golden Way</a>.<sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a aria-label=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-action=\"edit-section\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\" style=\"\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Cook\" title=\"David Cook\">David Cook</a> (August 1990). “Volume II”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Steve_Winter\" title=\"Steve Winter\">Steve Winter</a> ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Horde\" title=\"The Horde\">The Horde</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 108. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\">0-88038-868-4</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FF-p60-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-FF-p60_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Sehestedt\" title=\"Mark Sehestedt\">Mark Sehestedt</a> (2006). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Frostfell\" title=\"Frostfell\">Frostfell</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 60. ISBN <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-4245-2\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-4245-2\">0-7869-4245-2</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Edward_Bonny\" title=\"Edward Bonny\">Edward Bonny</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Brian_Cortijo\" title=\"Brian Cortijo\">Brian Cortijo</a>, <span class=\"new\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTGFzemxvX0tvbGxlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\" title=\"Laszlo Koller (page does not exist)\">Laszlo Koller</span> (November 2006). “The Horde: Barbarians of the Endless Waste”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Erik_Mona\" title=\"Erik Mona\">Erik Mona</a> ed. <a href=\"/wiki/Dragon_magazine_349\" title=\"Dragon magazine 349\"><i>Dragon</i> #349</a> (<a class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.paizo.com\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Paizo Publishing, LLC</a>), p. 58.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260514170052\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.064 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1084/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 4133/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1933/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 14/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2151/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/200\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   65.541      1 -total\n 65.40%   42.862      1 Template:Location\n 28.14%   18.444      1 Template:Refs\n  9.20%    6.027      1 Template:Cite_book/The_Horde/Volume_II\n  8.62%    5.651      2 Template:Cite_book\n  7.88%    5.166      3 Template:Cite_publication\n  5.62%    3.682      1 Template:Cite_dragon/349/The_Horde:_Barbarians_of_the_Endless_Waste\n  4.02%    2.636      1 Template:Cite_dragon\n  3.06%    2.007      1 Template:Cite_book/Frostfell\n  2.89%    1.892      1 Template:MakeUnionCatLink\n-->\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.8_prod_forgottenrealms:pcache:idhash:10787-0!sseVary=RegularPage!Fa